recorded 2026-11-14 9.0.10 neutralized
The T060 recording (read spike repeated on 2026-11-14) of ClientHelper op=clusterNodes (no details) with variant REST_90 and the 9.0.10 client on a non-production 9.0.10 node: 26 frames and one vendor log line on stdout, exit 0; the cluster keeps 21 nodes, 1 ACTIVE (the answering node) and 20 OFFLINE (version "-", uptime 0), zone and node ID "-" for every member. The vendor line right after start REST_90 is the 9.0 REST client's log4j2 line about netty's missing native DNS resolver library (research "Spike findings" T060); it names no host and is kept verbatim as recorded, outside the frames. Neutralized as in research D-26: the node names are replaced by node1 ... node21 in the recorded order (node1 = the answering node), the uptime of the ACTIVE node by a fictitious 86400000 ms; the nonce is the fixed fixture nonce; the version 9.0.10, the statuses and the vendor line are kept.
